    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. Can you go into a bit more detail on the 'gates' themselves? Especially for the transition from Testing to Staging and then from Staging to Production. I want to make sure we have enough safeguards in place so that unexpected errors or little glitches don't slip through the cracks and cause issues in the live environment.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the Testing to Staging transition, implement quality gates based on code coverage thresholds (e.g., >80%) and passing functional/integration test suites, ensuring the minimum required resilience is met. Before moving to Production, the Staging gate should include performance/load testing validation and a formal approval gate, often requiring stakeholder sign-off. Additionally, automated rollbacks should be a critical safety gate for the Production deployment itself.",
      "source": "target",
