    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Makes sense. One thing that worries me is how hard it is to catch those small, sneaky issues that don't show up in standard unit tests—you know, the kind of things that just seem to pop up out of nowhere and mess things up right when you think everything is solid. How can we harden these gates to make sure those \"hidden\" errors don't bypass our checks during the deployment process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
